summary:
  A station known to send plain FLAC still starts through the relay,
  because its address ends in .flac or the directory labels it FLAC.

history:
  An audition labelled FLAC and every address ending in .flac started
  through the relay. Measured on 2026-11-11: the stations the directory
  files as FLAC sent plain FLAC, which reached sound in 2.5 s straight off
  the socket with its ICY titles, and in 5.5 s through the relay with none.
  Only Ogg FLAC freezes without the relay, and only the stream's first
  bytes say which of the two a station sends; once they have said plain
  FLAC, the label and the ending no longer count.

target:
  package/contents/ui/KindLogic.js

find:
      if (known === "flac" || known === "other") return { relay: false, ask: false, pull: false };

replace:
      if (known === "other") return { relay: false, ask: false, pull: false };

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_kindlogic.qml::test_a_known_stream_starts_by_what_it_is.
  Line-neutral.
